.TH LIBUTF8_IS_VALID 3 LIBUTF8
.SH NAME
libutf8_is_valid - Test whether a codepoint is valid Unicode

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libutf8.h>

int \fBlibutf8_is_valid\fP(uint_least32_t \fIcodepoint\fP);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lutf8 .

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libutf8_is_valid ()
function tests whether a codepoint is valid Unicode.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR libutf8_is_valid ()
function returns 1 if the predicate is true, and 0 otherwise.

.SH ERRORS
The
.BR libutf8_is_valid ()
function cannot fail.

.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
